variants.description:
Top-ranked design (combined judge score 58, against 54.5 for D1 and 40.5 for D2). Q starts at 0. After prior_min_eps completed episodes the agent computes a level V from its own transitions. V is the closed-form TD(0) fixed point of a value function with one cell (every state lumped together) under the existing delayed-credit convention: V = EMA(sum of updated-pair rewards + g*r_done) / EMA((1-g)*n_updates + g), with n_updates = L-1. V is floored at 0 and ratcheted, so it only ever rises (running max). Each pair keeps W = prod(1 - alpha_k) over its own updates, so the stored value is Q = (zero-init EMA of observed targets) + W*V. While V is constant this is exactly Q-learning started at Q0 = V (verified algebraically by both judges). When V rises by dV, every row needs +W*dV. That shift is applied lazily: rowV[s] records the level row s already holds, a row is synced when it is read, and V changes only at episode end, so every row written in an episode was synced earlier in that episode.

Grafts:
- floor at 0 (J2);
- a full sync pass at the end of training (J1);
- Design 2's bias-corrected argmax as an evaluation-time A/B (prior_eval);
- int flags only, because AGENT_SET casts with type() and bool('0') is True;
- the M2 Q0=+3 run is reproducible as a diagnostic-only arm by presetting V, which also checks the implementation;
- no kappa/r_max and no level knob anywhere.

The default path is untouched: _train is not edited, and the prior runs in a separate _train_prior.

Arithmetic (mean random reward 0.075/step, crash at step L), random-phase level V at gamma 0.99:
- 1.25 / 3.35 / 5.0 for L = 100 / 200 / 400;
- 0 if mean episodes are shorter than 68 steps (the ratchet then holds today's behaviour until driving improves).

Levels at other gamma:
- 0.1-0.15 at gamma 0.5;
- 0.27-0.74 at 0.9;
- 2.2-37.5 at 0.999, at most 60 for crash-free speed 4, never 120.

Predictions (not yet run):
- gamma 0.99, T=60: 5.8-6.5 with alpha 0.1-0.2, and 5.5-6.0 with the tuned alpha schedule (current agent 5.32-5.61; M2 6.52).
- T=240: 7.1-7.7.
- gamma 0.999: 22.3 -> 24-30 (low confidence).
- gamma <= 0.95: unchanged within noise.

